hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1701","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who said: Narrated to us Salim ibn Nuh, who said: Narrated to us al-Jurayri, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\If three people set out on a journey"","" they should appoint one of them as their leader"","" and the most entitled to leadership among them is the one who is most versed in reciting the Qur'an.\""\n\nAbu Bakr (a narrator in the chain) said: This narration"","" along with the narration of Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id"","" and the narration of Aws ibn Dham'aj from Abu Mas'ud"","" indicates that if slaves are more versed in reciting the Qur'an than free men"","" they are more entitled to leadership. This is because the Prophet (ﷺ) did not exclude a free man over a slave in the narration.\n\n\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
